  "order": 1,
  "title": "Entra ID: users, groups, apps and managed identities",
  "summary": "Microsoft Entra ID is the identity directory behind Azure. Everything that can sign in is a principal in one Entra tenant: people as users, apps as service principals, Azure resources as managed identities. Subscriptions trust that tenant.",
  "notes": [
    "Users are members (your organisation) or guests (B2B: people from another tenant, who keep signing in with their own account).",
    "Groups collect users and service principals, so access can be granted once to the group instead of to each person.",
    "Workloads sign in as service principals. An app registration defines an app; its service principal is the app's identity inside a tenant (see the app registration pattern).",
    "Managed identities are service principals whose credentials Azure creates and rotates for you. System-assigned ones live and die with one resource; user-assigned ones are standalone and can be shared.",
    "Each subscription trusts exactly one tenant. Two separate permission systems sit on top: Entra roles control the directory itself (users, apps), and Azure RBAC controls Azure resources."
  ],
